e stated purpose is to prevent confusion about the meaning or depiction of hot spots.","narrative":"met als genoemd doel verwarring over de betekenis of weergave van hot spots te voorkomen","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The purpose is accurately attributed to the source as a stated aim, not a guaranteed outcome.","materiality":"This explains the reason given for standardization."},{"excerpt":"Zo kan de lezer begrijpen dat de markering niet één algemene betekenis heeft.","claim":"The shape distinction enables readers to understand that a hot spot marking does not have one general meaning.","category":"interpretation","label":"F1","evidence":"The FAA standardized two meanings with three shapes beginning May 19, 2022. A circle or ellipse marks a ground movement hot spot; a cylinder marks a wrong surface hot spot.","narrative":"Zo kan de lezer begrijpen dat de markering niet één algemene betekenis heeft.","narrativeRelation":"absent","origin":"independently_introduced","explanation":"The source establishes distinct meanings and symbols, but does not directly state what readers will understand; this is a reasonable, low-impact interpretation of the mappings.","materiality":"It adds a reader-understanding inference but does not materially alter the source's account."}]}

